Page 1691 Template:RQ:Doyle White Company/documentation: -------- begin text --------
{{documentation subpage}}

===Usage===
This template may be used in Wiktionary entries to format quotations from {{w|Arthur Conan Doyle}}'s work ''{{w|The White Company}}'' (1st US edition, 1891; 1st UK edition, 1891, 3 volumes). It can be used to create a link to online versions of the work at [https://books.google.com Google Books] and the [https://archive.org Internet Archive]:

* [https://archive.org/details/whitecompany00doyluoft/page/n10/mode/1up 1st US edition (1891)].
* 1st UK edition (1891):
** Volume I (not currently available online).
** [https://books.google.com/books?id=CJpJAQAAMAAJ&printsec=frontcover Volume II].
** [https://books.google.com/books?id=gKZJAQAAMAAJ&printsec=frontcover Volume III].


===Parameters===
The template takes the following parameters:

; 1st UK edition (1891)
* {{para|edition}} – '''mandatory''': if quoting from the 1st UK edition, specify {{para|edition|UK}}. If this parameter is omitted, the template defaults to the 1st US edition.
* {{para|volume}} – '''mandatory''': the volume number quoted from in uppercase Roman numerals, either {{para|volume|II}} or {{para|volume|III}}.

; Both editions
{{quote-meta/paramdoc|1=
<<chapter:1>>
<<page:2>>
<<passage:3>>
<<trailing_params>>
}}


===Examples===
; 1st US edition
* '''Wikitext''':
** {{temp|RQ:Doyle White Company|2=chapter=How a Champion Came forth from the East|3=page=309|4=passage=<nowiki>As he spoke, the knight-errant, who had remounted his '''war-horse''', galloped forward to the royal stand, with a silken kerchief bound round his wounded arm.</nowiki>}}; or
** {{temp|RQ:Doyle White Company|2=How a Champion Came forth from the East|3=309|4=<nowiki>As he spoke, the knight-errant, who had remounted his '''war-horse''', galloped forward to the royal stand, with a silken kerchief bound round his wounded arm.</nowiki>}}
* '''Result''':
** {{RQ:Doyle White Company|chapter=How a Champion Came forth from the East|page=309|passage=As he spoke, the knight-errant, who had remounted his '''war-horse''', galloped forward to the royal stand, with a silken kerchief bound round his wounded arm.}}

; 1st UK edition
* '''Wikitext''': {{temp|RQ:Doyle White Company|2=edition=UK|3=volume=II|4=chapter=How the Yellow Cog Fought the Two Rover Galleys|5=page=71|6=passage=<nowiki>"What was that?" he asked, as a hissing, sharp-drawn voice seemed to whisper in his ear. The steersman smiled, and pointed with his foot to where a short heavy cross-bow '''quarrel''' stuck quivering in the boards.</nowiki>}}
* '''Result''':
** {{RQ:Doyle White Company|edition=UK|volume=II|chapter=How the Yellow Cog Fought the Two Rover Galleys|page=71|passage="What was that?" he asked, as a hissing, sharp-drawn voice seemed to whisper in his ear. The steersman smiled, and pointed with his foot to where a short heavy cross-bow '''quarrel''' stuck quivering in the boards.}}

* '''Wikitext''': {{temp|RQ:Doyle White Company|2=edition=UK|3=volume=II|4=chapter=How a Champion Came forth from the East|5=pages=254–255|6=pageurl=254|7=passage=<nowiki>As he spoke, the knight-errant, who had remounted his '''war-horse''', galloped forward to the royal stand, with a silken kerchief bound round his wounded arm.</nowiki>}}
* '''Result''':
** {{RQ:Doyle White Company|edition=UK|volume=II|chapter=How a Champion Came forth from the East|pages=254–255|passage=As he spoke, the knight-errant, who had remounted his '''war-horse''', galloped forward to the royal stand, with a silken kerchief bound round his wounded arm.}}
