Page 3384 Template:RQ:Rowling Ickabog/documentation: -------- begin text --------
 {{documentation subpage}}
{{uses lua|Module:quote}}
{{RQ:Rowling Ickabog}}
==Usage==
This [[template]] may be used on Wiktionary entry pages to format quotations from [[w:The Ickabog|''The Ickabog'']] (2020) by [[w:J. K. Rowling|J. K. Rowling]].

===Parameters===
This template accepts the following parameters:
* {{para|year}}: '''Mandatory.''' The year the text was published. This [[parameter]] is alterable for various needs and circumstances.
* {{para|origyear}}: '''Optional.''' The year the text originated. Used when a newer edition of a text is quoted but the text is still largely unchanged.
* {{para|author}}: '''Mandatorily Included; Unalterable.''' Automatically, and unalterably, refers to {{w|J. K. Rowling}}.
* {{para|title}}: '''Mandatorily Included; Unalterable.''' Automatically, and unalterably, refers to {{w|The Ickabog}}.
* {{para|isbn}}: '''Optional.''' Defaults to the ISBN of the American edition, but can be altered to the British edition's ISBN number.
* {{para|publisher}}: '''Optional.''' Defaults to the American publisher, but can be altered to the British publisher of the text.
* {{para|chapter}}: '''Optional.''' The chapter the text segment being quoted is from.
* {{para|url}}: '''Optional.''' For linking to an online version of the text.
* {{para|edition}}: '''Optional.''' Refers to the edition being quoted (''e.g.'' 1st American Edition).
* {{para|format}}: '''Optional.''' Refers to the format the book is being processed in (''e.g.'' Paperback, Digital Format, ''etc.'')
* {{para|page}} or {{para|pages}}: '''Optional.''' The page number or pages being quoted.
* {{para|passage}}: '''Mandatory.''' The actual text segment being quoted from the book.
* {{para|footer}}: '''Optional.''' Adds a reference or a note to clear perceived confusion.

===Usage Notes 1===
See below to see common [[parameter]]s of this [[template]] in use.

===Example===
'''Wikitext''':
<pre>
#* {{RQ:Rowling Ickabog|chapter=Chapter 29: Mrs. Beamish Worries|url=https://dn790006.ca.archive.org/0/items/the-school-for-good-and-evil-books/The%20Ickabog%20by%20J.%20K.%20Rowling.pdf#page=149|page=131|passage=One let out a terrified giggle and another burst into tears.|footer=Footnote: In the physical, hardcover American edition, this is page 131, but online it is page 149.}}
</pre>

'''Result''':
#* {{RQ:Rowling Ickabog|chapter=Chapter 29: Mrs. Beamish Worries|url=https://dn790006.ca.archive.org/0/items/the-school-for-good-and-evil-books/The%20Ickabog%20by%20J.%20K.%20Rowling.pdf#page=149|page=131|passage=One let out a terrified giggle and another burst into tears.|footer=Footnote: In the physical, hardcover American edition, this is page 131, but online it is page 149.}}

===Usage Notes 2===
See below to see all [[parameter]]s of this [[template]] in use (with [[parameter]]s {{para|author}} and {{para|title}} exempt, from the fact that they are unalterable). Usage of [[parameter]] {{para|origyear}} is redundant, but for [[documentational]] purposes, is included nonetheless.

===Example 2===

'''Wikitext''':
<pre>
#* {{RQ:Rowling Ickabog|year=2020|origyear=2020|isbn=978-1-510-20225-2|publisher=[[wikipedia:London|London]]: [[wikipedia:Little, Brown and Company|Little, Brown Books for Young Readers]]|chapter=Chapter 47: Down in the Dungeons|url=https://dn790006.ca.archive.org/0/items/the-school-for-good-and-evil-books/The%20Ickabog%20by%20J.%20K.%20Rowling.pdf#page=221|edition=British 1st|format=Digital Format [ [[wikipedia:Internet Archive|Internet Archive]] ]|page=221|passage=In this way she kept busy, and tried to distract herself from her worries about Bert.|footer=Footnote: “She” refers to Mrs. Bertha Beamish.}}
</pre>

'''Result''':
#* {{RQ:Rowling Ickabog|year=2020|origyear=2020|isbn=978-1-510-20225-2|publisher=[[wikipedia:London|London]]: [[wikipedia:Little, Brown and Company|Little, Brown Books for Young Readers]]|chapter=Chapter 47: Down in the Dungeons|url=https://dn790006.ca.archive.org/0/items/the-school-for-good-and-evil-books/The%20Ickabog%20by%20J.%20K.%20Rowling.pdf#page=221|edition=British 1st|format=Digital Format [ [[wikipedia:Internet Archive|Internet Archive]] ]|page=221|passage=In this way she kept busy, and tried to distract herself from her worries about Bert.|footer=Footnote: “She” refers to Mrs. Bertha Beamish.}}

====Related Templates====
For other [[template]]s concerning the works of {{w|J. K. Rowling}}, see:
{{temp|RQ:Rowling Harry Potter}}, and {{temp|RQ:mul:Rowling Harry Potter}} (for non-English versions of {{w|Harry Potter}}).
