Page 4830 Template:RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong/passage boilerplate: -------- begin text --------
<noinclude>{{documentation}}</noinclude>This module is a data module providing a catalogue of passages from one particular book or article for each passage to demonstrate the existence of multiple {{{1|Pali}}} words.
The modules returns a 3-D array (technically a Lua table), indexed as follows:
# The outer index is the page number.
# The second index is a character string serving as the name of the passage within the page - using the first word is the simplest scheme.
# The third index is an element number  - the text (item 1), its transliteration (item 2) (optional) and its translation (item 3).  {{#ifeq:{{{nlt}}}|1|There are three optional items - normalisation, <!--
-->which corrects significant aberrant spelling or significant grammatical errors in the quoted text <!--
-->(item {{code|lua|norm}}), literal translation (item {{code|lua|lit}}), and normalisation of the <!--
-->transliteration (item {{code|lua|ts}}) to bring it into line with Roman script Pali.  <!--
-->The changed text is delimited by '''⧁⧀''' pairs so that it may be flexibly highlighted, <!--
-->and the effects should cascade from normalisation to transliteration to normalised transliteration.}}

The table has one named element, "reference", that holds the name of the template (namely, {{tl|{{{2|RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong}}}}}) used to identify the source to the reader and format the quote, its transliteration and its translation.
{{#if:{{{lang|}}}{{{p1|}}}{{{p2|}}}|
The table structure allows fields {{code|lua|lang}}, {{code|lua|p1}} and {{code|lua|p2}} for uninterpreted passage to the reference template to customise its output.  This particular module's table uses <!--
-->{{#if:{{{lang|}}}|{{code|lua|lang}} as the  <!--
  -->{{#ifeq:{{{lang}}}|1|language code of the quoted passage|{{{lang}}}}}<!--
  -->{{#if:{{{p1|}}}<!--
    -->|{{#if:{{{p2|}}}|, |&#32;and }}<!--
    -->|{{#if:{{{p2|}}}|&#32;and }}<!-- 
  -->}}<!--
-->}}<!--
-->{{#if:{{{p1|}}}|{{code|lua|p1}} as the {{{p1}}}<!--
  -->{{#if:{{{p2|}}}|&#32;and }}<!--
-->}}<!--
-->{{#if:{{{p2|}}}|{{code|lua|p2}} as the {{{p2}}}}}<!--
-->.  The field applied to the innermost of the passage, page and table is the value passed on.<br/><br/>
}}
The intention is that the word will be highlighted when selected by these three indices.  Words are assigned positive numbers and their boundaries are marked up in the form {number-word}.  This mark up can be nested, so that words may contain other words.  Different sections may have the same number; this allows for repeated words, overlapping words, and discontiguous translations.

The words are transcluded into a page using an invocation of the form {{tl|{{{2|RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong}}} quote|{{{3|241}}}|{{{4|namo}}}|{{{5|3}}}}}; this example produces the text:
{{{{{2|RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong}}} quote|{{{3|241}}}|{{{4|namo}}}|{{{5|3}}}}}

There is no advantage in including a passage for the sake of one word; one can use {{tl|{{{2|RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong}}}}} directly for that purpose.
<noinclude>{{tcat|lang=pi,okz,sa}}</noinclude>
-------- end text --------
Page 4830 Template:RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong/passage boilerplate: Skipped, no changes
Page 4831 Template:RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong/quote boilerplate: -------- begin text --------
This template is used to quote a passage from one particular publication to demonstrate the existence of {{#switch:{{padleft:|1|{{{1|Pali}}}}}|A|E|I|O|U=an|#default=a}} {{{1|Pali}}} word.  The passages are stored in [[{{{passages|Module:{{{2|RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong}}}}}}]], where the words are tagged by positive ID numbers; different passages have different numbering schemes. A quotation can be provided by an entry such as {{tl|{{{2|RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong}}} quote|{{{3|241}}}|{{{4|namo}}}|{{{5|4}}}}}.  The arguments mean use the quotation '{{{4|namo}}}' from page {{{3|241}}}, and embolden the word tagged as number {{{5|4}}}.  The result of this invocation is:

{{{{{2|RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong}}} quote|{{{3|241}}}|{{{4|namo}}}|{{{5|4}}}}}

If the word ID number is not used, then no words will be highlighted.  It is recommended that the value 0 be used for this option.  Thus, using '0' will result in:

{{{{{2|RQ:pi:Sai Kam Mong}}} quote|{{{3|241}}}|{{{4|namo}}}|0}}

The additional parameter {{para|brackets|on}} may be used to surround a quotation with [[bracket]]s. This indicates that the quotation either contains a mere mention of a term (for example, "some people find the word '''''manoeuvre''''' hard to spell") rather than an actual use of it (for example, "we need to '''manoeuvre''' carefully to avoid causing upset"), or does not provide an actual instance of a term but provides information about related terms.

<noinclude>{{tcat|lang=pi,nod,okz,sa}}</noinclude>
-------- end text --------
