Page 5333 Template:osa-att/documentation: -------- begin text --------
Attestation template for Old South Arabian inscriptions.

== Purpose ==

This template is used to cite attestations of Old South Arabian words and forms in inscriptions.

References should normally follow DASI (Database of South Arabian Inscriptions) conventions and use standard inscription sigla.

== Usage ==

Basic usage:

<pre>
{{osa-att|CIH 541}}
</pre>

Multiple attestations:

<pre>
{{osa-att|CIH 541|RES 3945}}
</pre>

With language identification:

<pre>
{{osa-att|CIH 541|lang=xsa}}
</pre>

With an editorial note:

<pre>
{{osa-att|CIH 541|note=Reading uncertain}}
</pre>

== Examples ==

Single attestation:

<pre>
{{osa-att|CIH 541}}
</pre>

→ Attested in CIH 541.

Multiple attestations:

<pre>
{{osa-att|CIH 541|RES 3945}}
</pre>

→ Attested in CIH 541 and RES 3945.

Language-specific attestation:

<pre>
{{osa-att|CIH 541|lang=xsa}}
</pre>

→ Attested in CIH 541 (Sabaic).

Attestation with note:

<pre>
{{osa-att|CIH 541|note=Reading uncertain}}
</pre>

→ Attested in CIH 541. Reading uncertain.

== Parameters ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter
! Description
! Required
|-
| <code>1</code>
| First inscription reference (e.g. <code>CIH 541</code>).
| Yes
|-
| <code>2</code>
| Additional inscription reference.
| No
|-
| <code>lang</code>
| Language of the attestation (e.g. <code>xsa</code>, <code>inm</code>, <code>xqt</code>, <code>xhd</code>).
| No
|-
| <code>note</code>
| Additional note displayed after the attestation.
| No
|}

== Notes ==

* Inscription sigla should follow [[Appendix:Old South Arabian inscription sigla]].
* Citation forms should generally follow DASI.
* Multiple attestations should be listed using standard inscription sigla.

== See also ==

* {{temp|R:DASI}}
* {{temp|R:Sabaweb}}
* [[Appendix:Old South Arabian inscription sigla]]
* [[Appendix:Old South Arabian bibliography]]

{{tcat|lang=inm|ref}}
-------- end text --------
