== "r" in German ==

On the appendix of IPA about German, the "r" is missing, there are two ways of pronouncing the "r" the one listed as in French and the one closer to Spanish "rr". I had add this change but it was removed, they are not the same. Pls don't change it [[User:Leo9469|Leo9469]] ([[User talk:Leo9469|talk]]) 19:35, 17 April 2022 (UTC)
: That's not a separate phoneme: it's just pronounced differently in different places. Allowing for different regional standards would be a lot more complicated than just adding a line for one variant. [[User:Chuck Entz|Chuck Entz]] ([[User talk:Chuck Entz|talk]]) 19:51, 17 April 2022 (UTC)
:{{re|Leo9469}} There is only one r-phoneme in German, which we transcribe {{IPAchar|/ʁ/}} and which can be pronounced {{IPAchar|[ʁ]}}, {{IPAchar|[r]}}, {{IPAchar|[ɐ̯]}} and a few other ways depending on factors like dialect and position in the syllable, but the German pronunciation appendix must not suggest that {{IPAchar|/ʁ/}} and {{IPAchar|/r/}} are separate phonemes in German, because they aren't. —[[User:Mahagaja|Mahāgaja]] · [[User talk:Mahagaja|''talk'']] 19:58, 17 April 2022 (UTC)

